# Five-state rules under Balzer's extra conditions (src/balzer.py)
# Conditions as reported by Mazoyer (Publ. Dept. Math. Lyon 1A, 1986, Sect. 7) and
# Yunes (thesis, Paris 7, 1993, Sect. 2.7):
#   B1 G stable, B2 image solution (involution I), B3 pre-firing GGG/*GG/GG* -> F, B4 G dominant.
# weak reading (conds 1234): B1 only for working neighbours; B3 without "only these produce F".
N=12    conds=1234 I=id  CaDiCaL with LRAT output stopped after 15 min (proof file > 2.7 GB);
        Kissat 4.0.4 without proof: UNSATISFIABLE in 16 min 6 s (2148 vars, 114965 clauses)
# strong reading (conds 1234s): B1 also for border neighbours; no other neighbourhood produces F.
# I(*)=*, I(F)=F, hence I(G)=G; I in {id, (A B), (L A), (L B)}.  Solver: CaDiCaL 3.0.1,
# certificates: LRAT (--lrat --binary=false), checked with lrat-check (drat-trim suite).
#
# weak reading
N=3..9  conds=1234 I=AB  SATISFIABLE (each < 4 s)
N=10    conds=1234 I=AB  UNSATISFIABLE 84.6 s  LRAT VERIFIED (380.1 MB, check 7.1 s)
N=3..8  conds=1234 I=LA  SATISFIABLE
N=9     conds=1234 I=LA  UNSATISFIABLE 37.1 s  LRAT VERIFIED (187.6 MB, check 3.5 s)
N=3..8  conds=1234 I=LB  SATISFIABLE
N=9     conds=1234 I=LB  UNSATISFIABLE 36.9 s  LRAT VERIFIED (184.4 MB, check 3.3 s)
N=3..11 conds=1234 I=id  SATISFIABLE (N=10: 156 s, N=11: 1.5 s); the N=11 rule
        (results/balzer_sym11_weak.txt) synchronizes 2..11 (fsspcheck), fails n=12 (fires at 21 < 22)
# strong reading
N=8..11 conds=1234s I=id SATISFIABLE; the N=11 rule (results/balzer_sym11.txt) satisfies
        all strong conditions, synchronizes 2..11 (fsspcheck), fails n=12 (fires at 20 < 22)
N=12    conds=1234s I=id UNSATISFIABLE 118.6 s LRAT VERIFIED (476.5 MB, check 8.5 s)
        (the strong reading is stronger than the weak one, so I=AB, LA, LB are refuted at N=10, 9, 9)
